+# Round 14 research report
+
+## Current checkpoint
+
+HEURISTIC work in progress (2026-10-19). The exact target is: for every fixed density alpha in (0,1/2], find c(alpha)>0 and an absolute exponent theta>1/4 such that every symmetric B in Z_q, q prime, excluding 0, with |B|/q=alpha+O(1/q), satisfies K=-min over gamma!=0 of sum over b in B of exp(2 pi i gamma b/q) >= c(alpha) q^theta. The permitted alternative deliverable is a precise obstruction to the proposed transfer of Sanders' half-set argument, including a counterexample or an identified missing step.
